WEBVTT

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:06.930
So I was sent by my boss to take pictures of the old castle theater before they tear it down.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:14.000
The real pictures of all that happened in this great old theater are etched in our hearts forever.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:15.650
Emily's right

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.750
Who could ever forget Sarah Bernhardt?

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.560
Blackwell, the greatest magician of this or any time.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.140
The beauteous Lillian Russell had.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:27.860
course.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.300
Mmm, my dear.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.100
A tragedian of superb talent.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.220
Your own unforgettable performances, Dr. Jekyll.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.200
And Mr. Hyde sent chills down my spine.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.010
I've got a few chills myself.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.710
Spider-sense chills.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:51.760
Hit!

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:52.970
It's alive!

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.370
You

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:03.320
What's all this nonsense about a ghost at the Castle Theater?

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.380
Well, it's like this, Mr. Jameson.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.520
Don't interrupt, Parker!

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.360
The Daily Bugle has been backing a citywide beautification campaign

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.620
to get rid of eyesores like that old termite tent show.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.420
I think ghosts are fun.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:20.760
And I saw the ghost too, only it disappeared before I could get a picture.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:21.460
Parker!

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.080
You're the victim of an underworked body and an overworked imagination.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:29.590
If I have my way, that theater will be torn down.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:30.460
starting

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:31.110
Go Ghost!

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:37.260
Okay, man.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.200
Here we go!

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:39.890
We'll be right back.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:52.810
What the hell?

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.200
Who's the wise guy?

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:02.560
You

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.710
B-b-b-b-boss, the place is haunted, let me out of here!

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:26.600
Guys

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:27.800
Wait for me!

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:34.030
Wait just a minute! I tell you, there's no such thing as ghosts!

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:38.460
I don't care how you do it, but tear down that building!

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:44.280
That theater is coming down, and there's not a ghost alive that can stop me!

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.280
A ghost alive? Now, there's an interesting idea.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.560
with these posters, they're really paper.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.000
Blackwell.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:22.660
He might have been able to pull those stunts off.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:29.940
My spider.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.900
senses of her tingling.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.710
Spider-Man only knew what was in store for him.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.180
The show is about to begin!

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.080
Pour off.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:03.430
The star performer...

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.160
Spider-Man!

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.300
So, Black Wolf.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.400
You are the one behind this.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:10.260
Of course!

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:12.540
Who else has my genius?

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.330
Your modesty overwhelms me.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.260
But what can you do for an encore?

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.580
I shall send you the dove of peace.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:31.360
Thank you.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.840
What up in web snappers?

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:06.840
Blackwell's flown the coop, too.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:11.360
Escape bundle?

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.530
Ah, but the best is yet to come.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:15.570
My spider senses are acting up again.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:21.240
Hold everything. Party's getting rough.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.480
Must be up there somewhere.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:29.240
He swallowed the baits.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:29.560
Sh...

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.200
See what happens.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.040
I know you're here, Blackwell. Come on out.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.870
I shall, Spider-Man, when it suits me!

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:38.990
Ha ha ha ha!

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:44.450
contract.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:46.870
No!

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.380
For my next treat!

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:58.100
What's the matter, Spider-Man?

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.680
They're only cannonballs!

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.940
I don't get a bang out of them.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.700
Let's see you presto yourself out of my web.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:08.800
If you insist.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.110
I'll show you a little trick I taught Houdini.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.080
My whips, he did it!

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.560
Offhand, my dear Emily, I'd say that Spider-Man has met his match.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:25.870
Thank you.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:34.200
I know it's a trick, but empty.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.510
But my spider sense...

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:37.660
Thank you.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.280
like confined quarters, Spider-Man.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:45.750
Very well.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.520
What a gripping scene!

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.070
Here, catch!

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:54.620
Do you ever miss?

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:55.590
Never!

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:04.000
Ha, ha, ha!

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:05.220
here I

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:06.620
I'm Spider-Man.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.160
Fun's fun, but the show's over, Blackwell.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:17.050
There's nothing like having a captive audience.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.010
James Booth.

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:21.580
and Emily Thorndike.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:27.340
Watch closely, Spider-Man, and you will see which of us has the greatest power.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.140
There's only one Blackwell.

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:35.400
Thank goodness.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.060
If he runs out of tricks, he can always get a job moving furniture.

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.370
Undeniably the greatest.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.100
I could enjoy it more if you'd point that thing the other way.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.900
Keep your eyes on the stage, Spider.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:00.220
Spider-Man.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:06.220
Down.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:08.040
Two.

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:09.110
One.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:10.520
Blast off.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.160
Show's over, folks.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.740
But it's a wooden prop gun and a rubber knife.

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:27.190
Correct, Spider-Man.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:29.650
This performance was for your benefit.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:33.420
Our motive to save the old castle theater.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.240
If you will champion our cause,

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:38.380
perhaps the theater can be spared.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.040
Will you help us?

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:42.370
It's a deal,

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:44.590
providing you'll do exactly what I say.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:48.090
First, we'll contact our rival newspaper.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.990
Unless worthy publication

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:53.670
in your Daily Bugle states that Spider-Man...

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:56.130
That arch-villain of society...

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.690
...has openly declared

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.970
that the castle theater should be taunt...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:09.060
down. He called our memories of yesteryear so much hogwash. Hogwash? Why that web-headed monster?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:17.510
I'll fix him. I, J. Jonah Jameson, dedicate my paper to the preservation of the old castle theater

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:24.400
for all posterity. But I thought you were backing the campaign to clear out all the old buildings.

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:29.980
I was only trying to point up their real value. You see, my...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.170
What an act old Jonah's got.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.700
Now I know what killed Vaudeville.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.750
Catches thieves, just like flies.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:04.750
Look out, here comes the Spider-Man.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:08.440
Is he strong? Listen, bud.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.620
He's got radioactive blood.

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.940
Can you swing from a thread?

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.080
Take a look overhead.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.460
Hey there, there goes the Spider-Man.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:23.640
A chill, the scene of a crime.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:28.470
Like a streak of light, he arrives just in time.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:29.810
Spider-Man.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.200
Spider-Man, friendly neighborhood Spider-Man

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.500
Wealth and fame, he's ignored

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:38.740
Action is his reward to him

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.150
Life is a great big hang-up

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:43.410
Wherever there's a hang-up

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.190
You'll find the Spider-Man
